<title>FIJI: Fiji sugar strike continues despite order to work.</title>
<headline>Fiji sugar strike continues despite order to work.</headline>
<dateline>SUVA 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Members of the Fiji Sugar and General Workers Union are continuing their week-old strike despite having been ordered by Fiji's Sugar Tribunal to return to work last Saturday at the nation's four sugar mills.</p>
<p>The Fiji Sugar and General Workers Union said on Monday it will file an appeal in the Suva High Court on Tuesday against the order issued by the Sugar Tribunal.</p>
<p>&quot;The workers want their demands on health and safety issues at Fiji Sugar Corporation met,&quot; union general secretary Felix Anthony told reporters.  </p>
<p>Before the strike, FSC had forecast Fiji's 1997 raw sugar production at 440,000 tonnes, down from 475,000 tonnes in 1996.</p>
<p>The 1997 crush had been running well before the strike, FSC said last week.</p>
<p>About 2,000 workers are on strike.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
